From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VirusBurst <VirusBurst@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:43:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] configs: x96q_lpddr3: set DRAM supply (DCDC3) to 1.2 V for
 LPDDR3

The X96Q LPDDR3 defconfig does not set CONFIG_AXP_DCDC3_VOLT, so the SPL
programs the AXP313 DCDC3 (vdd-dram) with the Kconfig default for
AXP313 of 1100 mV, which is meant for LPDDR4/LPDDR4X boards. LPDDR3
VDD2/VDDCA/VDDQ is specified at 1.2 V nominal (1.14 V minimum).

Both the U-Boot DT (sun50i-h313-x96q-lpddr3.dts) and the Armbian kernel
DT already declare reg_dcdc3 "vdd-dram" as fixed 1.2 V, so on a running
system Linux switches the rail to 1.2 V anyway, i.e. the DRAM is
currently trained by the SPL at 1.1 V and then operated at 1.2 V.
The Android boot0 on these boxes also sets DRAM_VCC to 1200 mV.

Set 1200 mV so that training and operation happen at the voltage the
memory is specified for. This was hardware-tested (memtester over 1 GiB,
1.5 GiB eMCP, both ranks) on a BA301_627 X96Q-type box. Boards with
DDR3/DDR3L use other defconfigs and are not affected.
---
 configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig b/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig
index e704130d..6bf4c394 100644
--- a/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig
+++ b/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ CONFIG_SUPPORT_EMMC_BOOT=y
 CONFIG_PHY_REALTEK=y
 CONFIG_SUN8I_EMAC=y
 CONFIG_AXP313_POWER=y
+CONFIG_AXP_DCDC3_VOLT=1200
 CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
